sentences.l:
and he in the dust on the ground fell, like a poplar
which in the water-meadow of a great marsh had grown,
smooth, but on its topmost part branches have grown;

“Rouse yourselves, horse-taming Trojans, and do not yield from the joy of battle
to the Argives, since not to them is stone the skin, nor iron,
to withstand the skin-cutting bronze, when they are hit;

and he on his back in the dust
fell down, both hands to his dear companions spreading out,
breathing out his life;

for there stood around him companions,
Thracians, topknotted, long spears in their hands holding,
who him, great though he was, and mighty, and noble,
pushed away from themselves;

So the two of them in the dust beside one another had been stretched out,
the one of the Thracians, the other of the bronze-shirted Epeans,
leaders;
